Background notification	Queue a notification after successful transfer.
Finish a complete backend service	WalletX combines Clean Architecture, CQRS/MediatR, EF Core, SQL Server, Swagger, Git workflow, debugging, and Hangfire. 
14. Conclusion
Recurring Jobs are a practical way to run scheduled work repeatedly without tying it to a user request. Hangfire provides the infrastructure for creating, storing, scheduling, processing, and monitoring these jobs. Cron expressions describe the schedule, while RecurringJob.AddOrUpdate() registers or updates the recurring definition.
For WalletX, the Daily Transaction Summary is a clear recurring task because it has business value, runs independently of an immediate API response, and can be verified easily through the Hangfire Dashboard. Alongside the post-transfer notification job, it demonstrates both scheduled and event-triggered background processing in the same backend.
